IMPORT prelude

-- State Immunity Act 1979 (Singapore) -- when a foreign State, or an entity of one, can be sued in a Singapore court, and what a
-- winning claimant can then do: general immunity and its exceptions (ss 3 to 9, 11, 13), service and default judgment (s 14),
-- relief and enforcement (s 15), who counts as a State and separate entities (s 16(1), (2), (4)), and excluded matters (s 19).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation "version in force from 1/4/2022", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SIA1979.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021";
-- the latest amendment annotated in the body is Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022 (the "notice of intention to contest or not contest"
-- wording in ss 2(2)(b), 3(2), 14).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0140 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The person here is someone with a claim against a foreign State or its agency -- a supplier, an embassy
-- employee, a landlord, someone injured -- and the question is whether the courts of Singapore will hear it and enforce it.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1(2), (3) (matters before 26 October 1979); s 4(6), (7) (appeals, counterclaims, authority to submit); s 8(3), (4);
-- s 10 (membership of bodies corporate); s 12 (Admiralty proceedings against ships and cargo); s 14(7) beyond its mention; s 15(1)
-- (no committal or fine for refusing disclosure) beyond this note; s 15(5) (the head of mission's certificate); s 16(3), (5), (6)
-- (separate entities that submit; federal constituent territories); s 17 (Presidential orders restricting or extending immunity);
-- s 18 (the Minister's conclusive certificate). Whatever immunity exists outside Part 2 (common law, diplomatic or consular
-- immunity) is not modelled: where Part 2 does not apply, this encoding says only that Part 2 does not apply.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `State Immunity Act 1979 -- immunity`

-- s 16(1): "The immunities and privileges conferred by Part 2 apply to any foreign or Commonwealth State other than Singapore; and
-- references to a State include references to -- (a) the sovereign or other head of that State in his or her public capacity; (b) the
-- government of that State; and (c) any department of that government, but not to any entity (called in this section a separate
-- entity) which is distinct from the executive organs of the government of the State and capable of suing or being sued."
DECLARE Defendant IS ONE OF
    `a foreign head of State acting in a public capacity`
    `a foreign head of State acting in a private capacity`
    `a foreign government`
    `a department of a foreign government`
    `a separate entity of a foreign State`
    `a private company`

-- What the proceedings are about. Each value names the exception in Part 2 that could apply, or none.
DECLARE Subject IS ONE OF
    `a commercial transaction`
    `a non-commercial contract to be performed in Singapore`
    `a contract of employment`
    `death, personal injury or damage to tangible property`
    `immovable property in Singapore`
    `property acquired by succession, gift or bona vacantia`
    `a Singapore patent, trade mark or design, or an infringement in Singapore`
    `an arbitration`
    `customs duty, excise duty or GST`
    `other taxation`
    `an exercise of sovereign authority`
    `criminal proceedings`
    `anything done by the State's armed forces in Singapore`

DECLARE Claim HAS
    `what the proceedings concern` IS A Subject
    `the State instituted the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State took a step in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the step was only to claim immunity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the step was taken in excusable ignorance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State agreed to submit after the dispute or in a prior written agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract is governed by Singapore law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties to the dispute are States` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties agreed otherwise in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in the State and governed by its administrative law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act or omission was in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the property is used for a diplomatic mission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State agreed in writing to arbitrate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arbitration agreement provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract was made in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the work is wholly or partly in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is now a national of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee was a Singapore citizen or resident when hired` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the work is for a commercial office of the State in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee was habitually resident in the State when hired` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Singapore law requires a Singapore court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `done in the exercise of sovereign authority` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `19 -- excluded matters`

-- s 19(2): "Part 2 does not apply to -- (a) proceedings relating to anything done by or in relation to the armed forces of a State
-- while present in Singapore ... (b) criminal proceedings; and (c) proceedings relating to taxation other than those mentioned in
-- section 13."
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 2 applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`'s `what the proceedings concern`
    WHEN `criminal proceedings` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `other taxation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `anything done by the State's armed forces in Singapore` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `4 -- submission to jurisdiction`

-- s 4(1): "A State is not immune as respects proceedings in respect of which it has submitted to the jurisdiction of the courts of
-- Singapore." (2): it may submit "after the dispute ... has arisen or by a prior written agreement; but a provision in any agreement
-- that it is to be governed by the law of Singapore is not to be regarded as a submission." (3): deemed to submit "(a) if it has
-- instituted the proceedings; or (b) ... if it has intervened or taken any step in the proceedings." (4): not a step "taken for the
-- purpose only of -- (a) claiming immunity". (5): not a step "taken by the State in ignorance of facts entitling it to immunity if
-- those facts could not reasonably have been ascertained and immunity is claimed as soon as reasonably practicable."
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the State has submitted` IF
        `the claim`'s `the State agreed to submit after the dispute or in a prior written agreement`
    OR  `the claim`'s `the State instituted the proceedings`
    OR  (    `the claim`'s `the State took a step in the proceedings`
         AND (NOT `the claim`'s `the step was only to claim immunity`)
         AND (NOT `the claim`'s `the step was taken in excusable ignorance`))

§§ `6 -- contracts of employment`

-- s 6(1): not immune "where the contract was made in Singapore or the work is to be wholly or partly performed in Singapore."
-- (2): the section does not apply if "(a) at the time when the proceedings are brought the individual is a national of the State
-- concerned; (b) at the time when the contract was made the individual was neither a citizen of Singapore nor habitually resident in
-- Singapore; or (c) the parties to the contract have otherwise agreed in writing."
-- (3): for "an office, agency or establishment maintained by the State in Singapore for commercial purposes, subsection (2)(a) and
-- (b) does not exclude the application of this section unless the individual was, at the time when the contract was made, habitually
-- resident in that State." (4): (2)(c) does not exclude it "where the law of Singapore requires the proceedings to be brought before a
-- court in Singapore."
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the nationality or residence bar applies` IF
        (   `the claim`'s `the employee is now a national of the State`
         OR (NOT `the claim`'s `the employee was a Singapore citizen or resident when hired`))
    AND (   (NOT `the claim`'s `the work is for a commercial office of the State in Singapore`)
         OR `the claim`'s `the employee was habitually resident in the State when hired`)

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employment exception applies` IF
        (`the claim`'s `the contract was made in Singapore` OR `the claim`'s `the work is wholly or partly in Singapore`)
    AND (NOT `the nationality or residence bar applies` `the claim`)
    AND (   (NOT `the claim`'s `the parties agreed otherwise in writing`)
         OR `the claim`'s `Singapore law requires a Singapore court`)

§§ `5, 7, 8, 9, 11, 13 -- the other exceptions`

-- s 5(1): not immune as respects "(a) a commercial transaction entered into by the State; or (b) an obligation of the State which by
-- virtue of a contract (whether a commercial transaction or not) falls to be performed wholly or partly in Singapore, but this
-- subsection does not apply to a contract of employment". (2): "This section does not apply if the parties to the dispute are States
-- or have otherwise agreed in writing; and subsection (1)(b) does not apply if the contract (not being a commercial transaction) was
-- made in the territory of the State concerned and the obligation in question is governed by its administrative law."
-- (3) "commercial transaction" means "(a) any contract for the supply of goods or services; (b) any loan or other transaction for the
-- provision of finance ... and (c) any other transaction or activity ... otherwise than in the exercise of sovereign authority."
-- s 7: death or personal injury, or damage to or loss of tangible property, "caused by an act or omission in Singapore."
-- s 8(1): "any interest of the State in, or its possession or use of, immovable property in Singapore"; (2) an interest "arising by
-- way of succession, gift or bona vacantia." s 19(1): "section 8(1) does not apply to proceedings concerning a State's title to or its
-- possession of property used for the purposes of a diplomatic mission."
-- s 9: (a) the State's own Singapore patent, trade mark or design; (b) "an alleged infringement by the State in Singapore".
-- s 11(1): where the State "has agreed in writing to submit a dispute ... to arbitration", not immune in proceedings "which relate to
-- the arbitration"; (2) "subject to any contrary provision in the arbitration agreement and does not apply to any arbitration
-- agreement between States."
-- s 13: "(a) any customs duty or excise duty; (b) any goods and services tax; or (c) any tax in respect of premises occupied by it for
-- commercial purposes."
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exception from immunity applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`'s `what the proceedings concern`
    WHEN `a commercial transaction` THEN
            (NOT `the claim`'s `the parties to the dispute are States`)
        AND (NOT `the claim`'s `the parties agreed otherwise in writing`)
    WHEN `a non-commercial contract to be performed in Singapore` THEN
            (NOT `the claim`'s `the parties to the dispute are States`)
        AND (NOT `the claim`'s `the parties agreed otherwise in writing`)
        AND (NOT `the claim`'s `made in the State and governed by its administrative law`)
    WHEN `a contract of employment` THEN `the employment exception applies` `the claim`
    WHEN `death, personal injury or damage to tangible property` THEN `the claim`'s `the act or omission was in Singapore`
    WHEN `immovable property in Singapore` THEN NOT `the claim`'s `the property is used for a diplomatic mission`
    WHEN `property acquired by succession, gift or bona vacantia` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Singapore patent, trade mark or design, or an infringement in Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an arbitration` THEN
            `the claim`'s `the State agreed in writing to arbitrate`
        AND (NOT `the claim`'s `the arbitration agreement provides otherwise`)
        AND (NOT `the claim`'s `the parties to the dispute are States`)
    WHEN `customs duty, excise duty or GST` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3, 16 -- who is immune`

-- s 3(1): "A State is immune from the jurisdiction of the courts of Singapore except as provided in the following provisions of this
-- Part." (2): the court gives effect to it "even though the State does not file and serve a notice of intention to contest".
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a State is immune under Part 2` IF
        `Part 2 applies` `the claim`
    AND (NOT `the State has submitted` `the claim`)
    AND (NOT `an exception from immunity applies` `the claim`)

-- s 16(2): "A separate entity is immune from the jurisdiction of the courts in Singapore if, and only if -- (a) the proceedings relate
-- to anything done by it in the exercise of sovereign authority; and (b) the circumstances are such that a State would have been so
-- immune."
-- A head of State in a private capacity and a private company are not "a State" under s 16(1): Part 2 gives them no immunity.
-- (Diplomatic immunity, preserved by s 19(1), is not modelled.)
GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Defendant, `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defendant is immune under Part 2` IF
    CONSIDER `the defendant`
    WHEN `a foreign head of State acting in a public capacity` THEN `a State is immune under Part 2` `the claim`
    WHEN `a foreign government` THEN `a State is immune under Part 2` `the claim`
    WHEN `a department of a foreign government` THEN `a State is immune under Part 2` `the claim`
    WHEN `a separate entity of a foreign State` THEN
            `the claim`'s `done in the exercise of sovereign authority`
        AND `a State is immune under Part 2` `the claim`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§ `State Immunity Act 1979 -- procedure and enforcement`

§§ `14 -- service and default judgment`

-- s 14(1): the originating document "must be served by being transmitted through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Singapore, to the
-- ministry of foreign affairs of that State, and service is deemed to have been effected when the writ or document is received at
-- that ministry." (2): any time for filing and serving a notice of intention to contest or not contest "begins to run 2 months after
-- the date on which the writ or document is so received." (3): a State which files and serves such a notice "cannot thereafter
-- object that subsection (1) has not been complied with". (4): "No judgment in default ... may be given against a State except on
-- proof that subsection (1) has been complied with and that the time ... as extended by subsection (2) has expired." (6): (1) does not
-- prevent service "in any manner to which the State has agreed and subsections (2) and (4) do not apply where service is effected in
-- that manner."  (5): the same 2 months runs from receipt of a default judgment before the time to set it aside starts.
GIVEN `served in a manner the State agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months after receipt before the time to respond starts` MEANS
    IF `served in a manner the State agreed` THEN 0 ELSE 2

GIVETH A NUMBER
`months after receipt of a default judgment before the time to set it aside starts` MEANS 2

GIVEN `served through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs` IS A BOOLEAN, `served in a manner the State agreed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the extended time has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 14(4) bars a default judgment` IF
        (NOT `served in a manner the State agreed`)
    AND (    (NOT `served through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs`)
         OR  (NOT `the extended time has expired`))

GIVEN `served through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs` IS A BOOLEAN, `served in a manner the State agreed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the State filed a notice of intention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the State may object to the manner of service` IF
        (NOT `served through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs`)
    AND (NOT `served in a manner the State agreed`)
    AND (NOT `the State filed a notice of intention`)

§§ `15, 16(4) -- relief and enforcement`

-- s 15(2): "(a) relief must not be given against a State by way of injunction or order for specific performance or for the recovery of
-- land or other property; and (b) the property of a State must not be subject to any process for the enforcement of a judgment or an
-- arbitration award or, in an action in rem, for its arrest, detention or sale." (3): this does not prevent relief or process "with the
-- written consent of the State concerned ... (which may be contained in a prior agreement) ... but a provision merely submitting to the
-- jurisdiction of the courts is not to be regarded as a consent". (4): "Subsection (2)(b) does not prevent the issue of any process in
-- respect of property which is for the time being in use or intended for use for commercial purposes."
-- s 16(4): "Property of a State's central bank or other monetary authority is not to be regarded for the purposes of section 15(4) as
-- in use or intended for use for commercial purposes".
-- s 15(1): no committal or fine for a State's failure to disclose or produce documents (not modelled further).
GIVEN `the State consented in writing to the relief` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an injunction or specific performance may be ordered against the State` IF
    `the State consented in writing to the relief`

GIVEN `the State consented in writing to enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN, `the property is in commercial use` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the property belongs to the central bank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the State's property may be seized to enforce a judgment` IF
        `the State consented in writing to enforcement`
    OR  (`the property is in commercial use` AND (NOT `the property belongs to the central bank`))
